--require spec_helper

# DO NOT ADD `--pattern` HERE. It reads like documentation and it silently breaks
# running one file: with a pattern configured, RSpec globs it and ignores the
# paths on the command line, so `rspec spec/models/site_spec.rb` runs the entire
# suite. Measured, not guessed.
#
# DO NOT ROOT THE DEFAULT PATH AT THE REPOSITORY (`--default-path .`) either. It
# was done once so an edition's specs were found, and it makes RSpec load every
# *_spec.rb under vendor/bundle on a CI runner, where gems install inside the
# checkout — bundler-audit's own specs among them.
